{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkLrbwXixNvBJ2TVVd6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't changed anything. This workspace has no GitLab access: I have no shell or GitLab API tools, and there's no `.git/config` remote I could find. The repository-security skill I have is for GitHub only, so I didn't use it for a GitLab project.\n\nYou can set it up yourself in either of these ways.\n\n**In the UI:** go to **Settings → Repository → Protected branches** and select **Add protected branch**.\n- Choose `main`.\n- Set **Allowed to merge** to Maintainers, or to specific roles or groups.\n- Set **Allowed to push and merge** to No one, so changes go through merge requests.\n- Leave **Allow force push** off.\n- On Premium or Ultimate, turn on **Require code owner approval** if you use CODEOWNERS.\n\n**Through the API:**\n```bash\ncurl --request POST --header \"PRIVATE-TOKEN: $GITLAB_TOKEN\" \\\n  \"https://gitlab.example.com/api/v4/projects/<PROJECT_ID>/protected_branches?name=main&push_access_level=0&merge_access_level=40&allow_force_push=false\"\n```\nHere `0` means no one and `40` means Maintainers. If `main` is already protected, this call returns a 409. In that case, delete the existing rule first or update it with `PATCH`.\n\nTo also require approvals and passing pipelines, set these under **Settings → Merge requests**:\n- Pipelines must succeed.\n- All threads must be resolved.\n- A minimum number of approvals. This is an approval rule and may need Premium.\n\nIf you want me to run this, I need three things from you:\n- The GitLab host and project path or ID.\n- A way to reach it, such as a shell with `glab` or `curl` and a token with the `api` scope.\n- The settings you want: who can merge, whether to require approvals, and whether to require code owners."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3870,"cache_read_input_tokens":8967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3870},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3aa13504-e088-4c99-b44a-d5acf0813a06","uuid":"2a31c09d-087b-44f7-8898-b622c3a8fc37","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:35:54.675Z","request_id":"req_011CgkLrbhtj7Ec4ZaQjcMsv"}
